# rmsd.in — backbone, ligand and binding-pocket RMSD
#
# Usage: cpptraj -i rmsd.in > rmsd.log 2>&1
# Replace SYSTEM, REP, LIG and POCKET_RESIDUES before running.
#
# Command order matters: the backbone line performs the superposition and
# modifies the frame coordinates; the nofit lines below inherit that alignment.

parm SYSTEM_dry.prmtop

# Reference for all RMSD values (cpptraj indexes frames from 1)
reference SYSTEM_prod_REP_dry.nc 1

trajin SYSTEM_prod_REP_dry.nc

# Global stability. Also provides the fit that removes translation/rotation.
rmsd backbone @CA,N,C out rmsd_backbone_REP.dat mass reference

# Ligand displacement relative to the protein. nofit prevents a second
# superposition, which would only report internal deformation of the ligand.
rmsd ligand :LIG out rmsd_ligand_REP.dat mass reference nofit

# Local stability of the binding site. Residue list from id_pocket_residues.in,
# kept identical across replicates.
rmsd pocket :POCKET_RESIDUES@CA,N,C out rmsd_pocket_REP.dat mass reference nofit

go

# Check in the log that each mask matched the expected number of atoms —
# a mask that matches nothing still produces an output file.
